The session files are written by hand for this repository on 2026-11-18 (CC0
1.0: no rights reserved; unit st-ses-i), in the Specctra session grammar that
KiCad's specctra_import.cpp reads, against the business card board's own part
and net names:
- business-card.ses: U1 placed where the board has it (150.9, 100.43, front,
  angle 0, resolution um 10, y negated as Specctra writes it); a through via
  padstack "Via[0-1]_600:300_um"; three nets: "unconnected-(U1-VSS-Pad4)"
  (three tracks from pad 4, F.Cu then B.Cu, and one via),
  "unconnected-(U1-VCC-Pad8)" (one track from pad 8) and "/NFC_ANT" (one
  track), the last a net the board lacks. KiCad counts 5 tracks, 1 via,
  3 nets, missing nets ["/NFC_ANT"].
- corrupt.ses: the first 900 bytes of business-card.ses, so KiCad's parser
  stops at its end.

business-card.kicad_pcb and business-card.kicad_pro are copies of the site
repository's frontend/src/public/services/kicad/fixtures/business-card/
(the owner's NFC business card; the SOURCE file there tells whose design it
is and where it comes from, and its terms, not CC0, hold for these two copies),
carried here so the island's e2e opens the same board:
business-card.kicad_pcb sha256 88c1bca11abfaabf22a14d0db6a02ff537822b62dc6b25a0f2c3175ddb7207c8
business-card.kicad_pro sha256 78ef903479c09c57e0f0f7e74916afeb748a5d884ca7e7927ba4e01fba182f64

